<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?><transcript><text start="2.8" dur="3.88">All right. So, this is a friend of mine</text><text start="5.24" dur="3.36">from Florida.</text><text start="6.68" dur="4">So, it&amp;#39;s it&amp;#39;s a nice coin like whatever,</text><text start="8.6" dur="4.24">but then on the other side it&amp;#39;s got a</text><text start="10.68" dur="4.28">nice little</text><text start="12.84" dur="4.88">You guys can see that, right?</text><text start="14.96" dur="4.68">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; All right. And so, I told him I said I</text><text start="17.72" dur="4.24">need to get this to the president. Can I</text><text start="19.64" dur="4.6">please have one to give to him? And so,</text><text start="21.96" dur="4.04">I was able to do it. And um but I just</text><text start="24.24" dur="3.68">want to welcome the president back to</text><text start="26" dur="3.64">his home state. Uh they&amp;#39;ve got a big</text><text start="27.92" dur="3.8">crowd in Fort Myers. I know a lot of</text><text start="29.64" dur="4.04">people are excited. Um we&amp;#39;ve got a lot</text><text start="31.72" dur="3.56">of races going on. And uh and I think</text><text start="33.68" dur="4.52">we&amp;#39;re going to do very well in Florida</text><text start="35.28" dur="4.16">as we have in recent years.</text><text start="38.2" dur="3.12">Great guy.</text><text start="39.44" dur="3">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; What&amp;#39;s your message to voters tonight</text><text start="41.32" dur="2.84">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Uh</text><text start="42.44" dur="2.88">just get out and vote. If they vote,</text><text start="44.16" dur="4.52">we&amp;#39;re going to win big.</text><text start="45.32" dur="5.12">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Any thoughts on the Alaska loss?</text><text start="48.68" dur="4.48">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, I&amp;#39;m the I&amp;#39;m the one that said do</text><text start="50.44" dur="5.08">it. They have two guys running named Dan</text><text start="53.16" dur="4.44">Sullivan running. So, the Democrats put</text><text start="55.52" dur="4.36">up a guy never pa- I don&amp;#39;t think he ever</text><text start="57.6" dur="4.76">voted before. All of a sudden he decides</text><text start="59.88" dur="3.88">to run for the Senate. And his name is</text><text start="62.36" dur="3.68">Dan Sullivan.</text><text start="63.76" dur="5.16">One is Daniel S. One is Daniel J. The</text><text start="66.04" dur="5.48">Daniel J. is the fake. And he wants to</text><text start="68.92" dur="4.24">change his middle initial to Daniel S.</text><text start="71.52" dur="1.84">But, he said this has nothing to do with</text><text start="73.16" dur="3.08">politics.</text><text start="73.36" dur="5.8">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; And and Daniel J. just so happens to be</text><text start="76.24" dur="4.04">funded by liberal donors. Imagine that.</text><text start="79.16" dur="3.64">What a coincidence that is.</text><text start="80.28" dur="3.88">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; By By ActBlue. Okay. But, he has nothing</text><text start="82.8" dur="2.08">to do with politics. No, it&amp;#39;s a</text><text start="84.16" dur="2.08">disgrace.</text><text start="84.88" dur="3.08">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Governor, how do you think the Florida</text><text start="86.24" dur="2.96">turnout will be tonight? Why did Why did</text><text start="87.96" dur="2.92">so much go down?</text><text start="89.2" dur="3.72">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, look. I mean, I I think anytime</text><text start="90.88" dur="4.08">you run as a first-time candidate, it&amp;#39;s</text><text start="92.92" dur="4.28">a big state. You got to get known. That</text><text start="94.96" dur="5.28">just takes time. But, if you look when I</text><text start="97.2" dur="4.88">ran uh 8 years ago, we had 300,000 more</text><text start="100.24" dur="5.24">registered Democrats in this state than</text><text start="102.08" dur="5.2">Republicans. Today, we have 1.5 million</text><text start="105.48" dur="3.44">more registered Republicans. So, I think</text><text start="107.28" dur="4.32">what the president said is right. If</text><text start="108.92" dur="4.36">people come out, if our people vote, I</text><text start="111.6" dur="3.24">think we&amp;#39;ll win not just in Florida, but</text><text start="113.28" dur="3.8">some of these other Senate races that</text><text start="114.84" dur="4.28">are close, if our people show up, we&amp;#39;ll</text><text start="117.08" dur="3.68">win those Senate races. Uh so, it&amp;#39;s all</text><text start="119.12" dur="3">about the turnout, and no one does it</text><text start="120.76" dur="1.92">better than the president of the United</text><text start="122.12" dur="1.84">States.</text><text start="122.68" dur="2.76">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Mr. President, you&amp;#39;re in fast</text><text start="123.96" dur="2.6">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; He&amp;#39;s He&amp;#39;s going to be in great shape.</text><text start="125.44" dur="2.8">He&amp;#39;s going to be in great shape.</text><text start="126.56" dur="4.48">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Your ambassador to Turkey, sir, just</text><text start="128.24" dur="4.48">said in an interview that, absolutely,</text><text start="131.04" dur="4.2">{quote} {unquote}, there could be a</text><text start="132.72" dur="4.84">strike on Iran this weekend. Have you</text><text start="135.24" dur="4.56">gone back on holding off on relaunching</text><text start="137.56" dur="4.96">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; my ambassador to Turkey. He&amp;#39;s a pretty</text><text start="139.8" dur="4.24">powerful man, I guess. Well, if if</text><text start="142.52" dur="3.08">that&amp;#39;s the case, I don&amp;#39;t know anything</text><text start="144.04" dur="2.76">about it. Thank you very much,</text><text start="145.6" dur="3.359">everybody. Run, thank you.</text><text start="146.8" dur="4.72">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you, sir.</text><text start="148.959" dur="2.561">Say hello to your</text></transcript>